Database Conventions

## Slide 2

Tables

Database Conventions

Table Naming
TrakSYS Table names begin with t
tArea
tSystem
tJob
Etc…

Foreign Key Convention
Naming…
Typically, RelatedTableNameID
In some cases, PrefixRelatedTableNameID

Unique Identifier
Nearly all TrakSYS tables contain a unique ID Column
(there are a few exceptions)

## Slide 3

Views, Stored Procedures and Functions

Database Conventions

Naming
TrakSYS View names begin with view
viewEvent
viewJob
Etc…
TrakSYS Stored Procedure names begin with sp
spCore_Sequence_NextID
spUpdateOeeInterval
Etc…
TrakSYS Function names begin with uf
ufConvertIntToColorHex
ufGetDateValue
Etc…

## Slide 4

Sequences

Database Conventions

Never!
Attempt to determine the next ID by MAX
Manipulate the tSequence Table

Manual Record Creation
When creating (inserting) records into TrakSYS tables without using the API, special care must be taken!
Api.Util.Db.GetNextSequenceByKey
spCore_Sequence_NextID_Out

Overview
tSequence stores the highest ID value (last) for each TrakSYS Table
New IDs are assigned and managed from within TrakSYS
API DB Objects automatically create new IDs on Insert

